X:1
T:Here Comes the Rain Again
C:Annie Lennox and Dave Stewart (Eurythmics)
M:4/4
O:England, 1984
N:First verse and the chorus build-up. Melody from the vocal channel (a pan-flute line, channel 3) of a MIDI karaoke arrangement (hamienet.com, track 15770); the other three Rain Again files there are copies of the same data, and track 4107 has no vocal line, so there is no independent cross-check. Transposed down a fifth from C to F major, so the range is D4 to C5. Chords from the bass channel (an Am-F-G ostinato in the verse, F-C in the chorus), shifted the same way. The arrangement gates notes short (an eighth sung as a sixteenth); notes are written to the next onset when the gap is half a beat or less, and longer gaps stay as rests. The verse is followed here by the lead-in bar of the chorus; the second verse is skipped. The last bar holds the final note and the loop returns to the verse.
